{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1136473-abominations","id":1136473,"title":"Abominations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-01T19:18:18-07:00","id":1136473,"title":"Abominations","content":"So an Abomination can pretty much use Crinos form with discipline right?<br /> <br /> I been reading up on Abominations and they seem to be extraordinarily powerful.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T19:54:51-07:00","id":1136474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicballz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1136473-abominations#post1136473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So an Abomination can pretty much use Crinos form with discipline right?<br /> <br /> I been reading up on Abominations and they seem to be extraordinarily powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yes and No. They lose auto healing. They take agg from Silver as well as standard Kindred issues. They Lose Rank even if they are BSDs. They are in a constant state of Harano. I'm not sure if they even still get Rage though if they do that's far more useful than a couple of dots of strength.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T20:10:23-07:00","id":1136475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicballz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1136473-abominations#post1136473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So an Abomination can pretty much use Crinos form with discipline right?<br /> <br /> I been reading up on Abominations and they seem to be extraordinarily powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are immensely powerful but constant Harano + the combo of werewolf and vampire weaknesses mean they aren't an incredibly fun play experience unless you're REALLY into the tragedy of their existence (powergamers will be disappointed when the sunlight issue takes them out of play half the time relative to other shifter characters, for example). They're wmds as npcs, but (while playable) clearly not designed as optimized pcs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T21:36:55-07:00","id":1136491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1136473-abominations?p=1136474#post1136474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Yes and No. They lose auto healing. They take agg from Silver as well as standard Kindred issues. They Lose Rank even if they are BSDs. They are in a constant state of Harano. I'm not sure if they even still get Rage though if they do that's far more useful than a couple of dots of strength.</div> </div> </div> </div>Abominations retain Rage but cannot use it along with blood or Gnosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T23:34:49-07:00","id":1136503,"title":"","content":"Are Abominations that bad that their existence is a tragedy? In most series, Hybrids are more powerful than either side. EX: Underworld, TVD, THe ORiginals and etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T01:21:43-07:00","id":1136517,"title":"","content":"Their existence is a mixture of Werewolf Rage and the Vampire Beast calling to them all at once. They were servants of Gaia, holy warriors of earth. Now they're some... well abomination. They are powerfull, when confronted directly. They have Disciplines, Rage, Gifts and whatnot, but they are feeling the call of two extremely different destinys. They can't follow one whithout abandoning the other. The more they grow in power, the more they lose their werewolf conscience to their corrupted vampire side.<br /> Think a vampire is damned? This destiny is the worst imagenable for a werewolf.<br /> <br /> Even in terms of raw power, they're impressive, yes. But they're also quite full of weaknesses. No auto healing means they need to heal with blood points, which limits their healing capabilities and prevents them from using gifts/rage the same turn. Only one ressource can be tapped at one time. Silver, sunlight, even normal fire and stakes are your enemies. You're powerfull, sure. But your weaknesses increase by the same amount.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T16:30:05-07:00","id":1136746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicballz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1136473-abominations?p=1136503#post1136503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Abominations that bad that their existence is a tragedy? In most series, Hybrids are more powerful than either side. EX: Underworld, TVD, THe ORiginals and etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, because they go from being a creature that is more alive than any human being will ever understand to being a dead thing that is, by every idea they used to believe in (and often had objective proof of its truth), is damned, and they are that way because of their own personal failure. (Things like Underworld and the like usually don't have the spiritual aspect to werewolves that W:tA makes a cornerstone of the Garou's existence.)<br /> <br /> Mechanically, being in a state of perpetual Harano means that all of an Abomination's dice pools are halved, unless they spend a Willpower point to pull them selves out of it for a Scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T17:52:10-07:00","id":1136770,"title":"","content":"Abominations are things which should feel like insane wrecking balls which are pitiful rather than enjoyable.<br /> <br /> NO ONE PLAYS THEM LIKE THIS.<br /> <br /> As such, I have the rule Garou who are embraced just die or they become vampires and lose all of their former abilities.<br /> <br /> &quot;Ex-Garou&quot; are usually psychotically hateful to their brethren, suicide, or both.<br /> <br /> They do, however, get Protean as a Clan Discipline.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T20:47:57-07:00","id":1136811,"title":"","content":"My favorite was always how it was decided that the Mokole would go completely berserk and destroy everything around themselves in godzilla form before finally bursting into flames.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T22:59:05-07:00","id":1136841,"title":"","content":"Abomination PCs aren't really stronger then normal Garou, they have perma depression and stunted healing factors. But they can really excel as an NPC, particularly if you use one as a Big Bad as they can become a meat puppet for the Maeljin removing their crippled soul status, which is funny since they never really explored this in the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T15:32:14-07:00","id":1137070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicballz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1136473-abominations?p=1136503#post1136503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Abominations that bad that their existence is a tragedy? In most series, Hybrids are more powerful than either side. EX: Underworld, TVD, THe ORiginals and etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>The examples you provide feature generic werewolves, not Garou. Garou have only superficial similarities to typical Hollywood movie werewolves; they become wolves and wolfmen, and sometimes travel in packs. Beyond that, it's best to not think of the two things as the same. Underworld's &quot;Hybrids&quot; are nothing at all like an Abomination, because the things that make them what they are have massive fundamental differences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T20:24:00-07:00","id":1137174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1136473-abominations?p=1136841#post1136841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abomination PCs aren't really stronger then normal Garou, they have perma depression and stunted healing factors. But they can really excel as an NPC, particularly if you use one as a Big Bad as they can become a meat puppet for the Maeljin removing their crippled soul status, which is funny since they never really explored this in the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most likely because the post-Skins writing for Samuel Haight ensured that we can't have nice things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T20:55:15-07:00","id":1137179,"title":"","content":"Well, vampires are supposed to have a miserable existence if they're a decent person and only enjoy themselves if they're psychopaths.<br /> <br /> Garou are like that but have proof, positive God is real and God hates what you are.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> One game which I think did a decent job of using Abominations in the game is the fact the Camarilla and Sabbat BOTH forbid the embracing of Garou. Why? Because when you have what is already a violently unstable monster and then make it a violently unstable UNDEAD monster, it's basically a one-man wrecking ball which automatically enters wassail or is likely to kill and kill until it does.<br /> <br /> In his game, Abominations had a -1 penalty for Frenzy to EVERY point of Rage they had.<br /> <br /> Any game involving Abominations basically amounted to, &quot;Follow the various locations where the Garou murdered six to a dozen people and explain to the police why there's no memory of what killed all these people.&quot;<br /> <br /> I also threw in the additional fact that massive amounts of Banes were attracted to Abominations so WEIRD STUFF HAPPENS around them. Street lights all go out, car alarms activate, cars start driving at you, steam pipes burst and more.<br /> <br /> It's basically a ace to save the Masquerade and keep the bodies in the hundreds as they kill everything until either dying in Sunrise or (God help you) they hide in the sewers or learn to survive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-04-2017, 01:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T12:42:47-07:00","id":1137791,"title":"","content":"Abominations are powerful, they have more powers to work with and while they also may have more weaknesses, said powers are perfectly capable of compensating for or outright removing said weaknesses(on both sides, werewolves have high level gifts that remove weakness to silver, vampires have immune to fire blood magic rituals etc.).<br /> <br /> The main thing that limits this from full munchkin is the facts that A. xp is limited(basic design philosophy of CWOD, as opposed to the D&amp;D esc &quot;xp is a river&quot;), B. they have to survive long enough to buid any power(no allies on either side means no trustworthy teachers, they live in a decaying spiral of harano and gnosis loss that weakens them with time, and the have limited ways of regaining their resources without being found out) and C. their basic ideas of morality that they've been raised with and proven to are antithetical to their very existence(more so than a vampire's humanity).<br /> <br /> There is no way for an abomination to survive without not only abandoning everything it believes, but also becoming a villian more horrible than any they've ever fought. They'd need to join the wyrm to keep their gnosis, they'd need to devour the souls of vampires to have enough power to not be hunted down, they'd need to survive in a world that want s to kill them by destroying anyone that got in the way. This makes them horrible fits as PC, unless of course your particular PC Wants to play the rise of one of the most evil being in history and one of the beings responsible for the WOD being as crappy as it is for everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T15:11:45-07:00","id":1137840,"title":"","content":"For maximum Survival sell your soul to the Yama Kings, become a greater Akuma. They'll keep your soul nice and safe! You get new powers. You probably won't be a slave to the beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T17:05:38-07:00","id":1137871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1136473-abominations?p=1137840#post1137840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For maximum Survival sell your soul to the Yama Kings, become a greater Akuma. They'll keep your soul nice and safe! You get new powers. You probably won't be a slave to the beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yama Kings can't support primal Gnosis, so they probably can't do that. This is explicitly noted in The 1000 Hells - Changers who enter truck with the Yama Kings lose their spirit-related powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T19:45:35-07:00","id":1137901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1136473-abominations?p=1137871#post1137871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yama Kings can't support primal Gnosis, so they probably can't do that. This is explicitly noted in The 1000 Hells - Changers who enter truck with the Yama Kings lose their spirit-related powers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While this is true since your gnosis is your path you're already going to be losing that just by acting. And it can't be regained. So inevitably you're going to lose it. So why not trade it in for fabulous fun and prizes! Become like one of the Animal Generals. SO rage, Kindred discplines, KJ Discplines, Infernal Investments... for those who want to spit in the face of a Gaia who allowed you to be embraced its pretty spectacular.<br /> <br /> Personally I'd still pick the Eye of Heaven but you know I might pick that as a human who got embraced anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T14:32:41-07:00","id":1155858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1136473-abominations?p=1137901#post1137901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While this is true since your gnosis is your path you're already going to be losing that just by acting. And it can't be regained. So inevitably you're going to lose it. So why not trade it in for fabulous fun and prizes! Become like one of the Animal Generals. SO rage, Kindred discplines, KJ Discplines, Infernal Investments... for those who want to spit in the face of a Gaia who allowed you to be embraced its pretty spectacular.<br /> <br /> Personally I'd still pick the Eye of Heaven but you know I might pick that as a human who got embraced anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you do it during silk road, you could also steal from devil's due and convert your gnosis to resolve/torment. With daimoinon 6 you also get 10 points of arcana per dot in daimoinon.<br /> <br /> As per books of the wyrm, freakes legion, and wta possessed you can force a bane to possess you and enjoy the powers of a fomori for free(unless it's a spirit of blood or death the bane can't take control).<br /> <br /> If we use tal'mahe'ra: guide to the black hand you can dominate a nephandi to be your blood familiar and gain access to pillars/spheres<br /> <br /> as per WTO: mediums you can get spectre bestowments of the first dot of any arcanoi(side powers included).<br /> <br /> So this totals at getting access to KJ/Kindred disciplines, gifts, infernal investments(wyrmish, inferno, arcanoi and devil's due arcana), possessed powers, keeping you gnosis as demonic resolve, and nephendi awakened magic.<br /> <br /> Anyone know why the demons haven't won yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 11-04-2017, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T15:02:32-07:00","id":1155868,"title":"","content":"Because there is no way to satisfy all the obligations you are now bound to, plus you cannot be possessed by anything. I'm fairly certain that you also cannot have Kindred Disciplines and KJ disciplines at the same time (the powers of Caine and the powers of the Yama being mutually exclusive). Also as an abomination you REALLY do not want to convert your Gnosis to anything since at that point you cannot use Gifts, Fetishes or step sideways (although stepping sideways is crazy dangerous due to the light of Helios permeating the Umbra). At some point in the midst of all this the character is no longer a character anyway and has long since become an NPC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T18:03:15-07:00","id":1155905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1136473-abominations?p=1155868#post1155868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because there is no way to satisfy all the obligations you are now bound to, plus you cannot be possessed by anything. I'm fairly certain that you also cannot have Kindred Disciplines and KJ disciplines at the same time (the powers of Caine and the powers of the Yama being mutually exclusive). Also as an abomination you REALLY do not want to convert your Gnosis to anything since at that point you cannot use Gifts, Fetishes or step sideways (although stepping sideways is crazy dangerous due to the light of Helios permeating the Umbra). At some point in the midst of all this the character is no longer a character anyway and has long since become an NPC.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the NPC thing happened at the word abomination. However to answer some of your points, 1000 hells detail that the yama kings can grant kuei jin disciplines even to creature that normally couldn't possess them(in fact one of the &quot;legendary akuma&quot; is in fact kindred). Devil's due specifically states you Do use the now converted resolve for all things gnosis was once used for.<br /> <br /> Though all of this is has a requirement of &quot;So evil nephendi think you're screwed up&quot; and thus would be storyteller characters. I would however like to point out that in a one world of darkness setting the infernalist factions(nephendi, wyrm, inerno-demons, fallen, etc.) would eventually spawn one of these crimes against nature by the simple facts of it's mechanically possible/there are reasons in fluff for it to happen and someone out in WOD will be screwed up enough to pull it off(Look at sam height, the joke of WTA for example)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T18:55:22-07:00","id":1155914,"title":"","content":"You might see one, ever, given how hard it is for an Abomination to ever get made in the first place. You are talking about something as rare as the a Herald of the Green Dragon, The First Ronin &amp; The Perfect Metis. Even then with all the toys you need to spend a WP point in any scene you want more than half dice pools and can't ever spen WP on a roll for a success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T04:04:17-08:00","id":1155998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1136473-abominations?p=1155914#post1155914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might see one, ever, given how hard it is for an Abomination to ever get made in the first place. You are talking about something as rare as the a Herald of the Green Dragon, The First Ronin &amp; The Perfect Metis. Even then with all the toys you need to spend a WP point in any scene you want more than half dice pools and can't ever spen WP on a roll for a success.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, never understood the craze about abominations.<br /> <br /> A vampiric fomori has all the same powers and more but with no harano, silver weakness, and can take the &quot;regeneration&quot; ability so that it works for them despite being undead. A wyrm infernalist is still going to be hunted by the sabbat and the bane inside it's going to screw him with taints any chance it gets after it learns it can't take over(unless it's a bane of blood or death, in which case case I hope the infernalist likes taking a back seat in his own head.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T07:42:48-08:00","id":1156048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1136473-abominations?p=1155998#post1155998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, never understood the craze about abominations.</div> </div> </div> </div>At a guess, confusing <i>what</i> you are rather than <i>who</i> you are as what makes you unique. That and getting to have two sets of super powers at once. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T03:13:42-08:00","id":1157727,"title":"","content":"Abominations are unbelievably powerful, it's best that they are not played as player characters though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11698,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11698-darko","user":"Darko","date":". 11-11-2017, 06:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11698-darko","name":"Darko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11698_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T07:48:30-08:00","id":1157750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1136473-abominations?p=1157727#post1157727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abominations are unbelievably powerful, it's best that they are not played as player characters though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Disagree.<br /> <br /> First, they are not that powerful. As Werewolves, they lost more than they got. I mean, Werewolf regeneration is great, and their Gnosis is going to plummet now. They get few things in the trade, and the best is simply <i>access</i> to a new set of powers. You still need XP to develop Disciplines, so you basically gives up on spending XP on Gifts to spend it on Disciplines. It is a good trade for a beginner, but not so great for a higher Rank Werewolf.<br /> <br /> Second, they are just impractical to play, and seriously, they are a good concept. They could be weaker and they would still be an interesting concept. I already waved the Gnosis Harsh Rules on a game and let a PC Abomination with Humanity, and it went well. It wasn't a common chronicle, it started at a little higher level (Rank 3 for Werewolves, 7th Generation for Vampires without Gen being available as Background), but it went smoothly nonetheless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T10:03:33-08:00","id":1157776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1136473-abominations?p=1157750#post1157750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disagree.<br /> <br /> First, they are not that powerful. As Werewolves, they lost more than they got. I mean, Werewolf regeneration is great, and their Gnosis is going to plummet now. They get few things in the trade, and the best is simply <i>access</i> to a new set of powers. You still need XP to develop Disciplines, so you basically gives up on spending XP on Gifts to spend it on Disciplines. It is a good trade for a beginner, but not so great for a higher Rank Werewolf.<br /> <br /> Second, they are just impractical to play, and seriously, they are a good concept. They could be weaker and they would still be an interesting concept. I already waved the Gnosis Harsh Rules on a game and let a PC Abomination with Humanity, and it went well. It wasn't a common chronicle, it started at a little higher level (Rank 3 for Werewolves, 7th Generation for Vampires without Gen being available as Background), but it went smoothly nonetheless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Abominations do have a good concept, but they are more useful as storyteller-device than actual player characters. They are actually powerful and even the book authors agree with that, it's a fact. For example, an Abomination with only Celerity 5 is already very powerful (you can soak any type of damage if you're in a form that's not your breed; and any form if you're Metis. Plus, you can have 5 extra actions instead of a maximum of permanent Rage rating/2. You also can remain active. If you don't spend extra actions you already have +5 dice to your Dexterity-related actions; believe me, that's a lot of dicepool). Not to mention if the said Abomination had Spirit of the Fray or any other Gift that's alike, it would make them really unbeatable in combat (could probably even take on an experienced werewolf elder on a one versus one combat). Adding an Abomination as a player character can really break the game if it's not monitored and started properly, that's just my little humble opinion and I respect yours as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11698,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11698-darko","user":"Darko","date":". 11-11-2017, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11698-darko","name":"Darko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11698_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T11:15:00-08:00","id":1157793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1136473-abominations?p=1157776#post1157776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Abominations do have a good concept, but they are more useful as storyteller-device than actual player characters. They are actually powerful and even the book authors agree with that, it's a fact. For example, an Abomination with only Celerity 5 is already very powerful (you can soak any type of damage if you're in a form that's not your breed; and any form if you're Metis. <b>Plus, you can have 5 extra actions instead of a maximum of permanent Rage rating/2</b>. You also can remain active. If you don't spend extra actions you already have +5 dice to your Dexterity-related actions; believe me, that's a lot of dicepool). Not to mention if the said Abomination had Spirit of the Fray or any other Gift that's alike, it would make them really unbeatable in combat (could probably even take on an experienced werewolf elder on a one versus one combat). Adding an Abomination as a player character can really break the game if it's not monitored and started properly, that's just my little humble opinion and I respect yours as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, Rage doesn't technically cap the number of actions that you can get, just the points that you can spend. This is an important distinction when you get to a Gift like Rage of the Many-Taloned Hunter, which counts each Rage point you spend to gain extra actions as two. The principle limit, however, is still the lower of Dexterity or Wits (or just Dexterity in a frenzy), since moving faster than your coordination can manage inflicts a +3 difficulty penalty to all your rolls for that turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T11:42:28-08:00","id":1157798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1136473-abominations?p=1157776#post1157776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abominations do have a good concept, but they are more useful as storyteller-device than actual player characters. They are actually powerful and even the book authors agree with that, it's a fact. For example, an Abomination with only Celerity 5 is already very powerful (you can soak any type of damage if you're in a form that's not your breed; and any form if you're Metis. Plus, you can have 5 extra actions instead of a maximum of permanent Rage rating/2. You also can remain active. If you don't spend extra actions you already have +5 dice to your Dexterity-related actions; believe me, that's a lot of dicepool). Not to mention if the said Abomination had Spirit of the Fray or any other Gift that's alike, it would make them really unbeatable in combat (could probably even take on an experienced werewolf elder on a one versus one combat). Adding an Abomination as a player character can really break the game if it's not monitored and started properly, that's just my little humble opinion and I respect yours as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>The caviat being that an abomination has to Survive long enough to get to celerity 5. That's the kicker, they don't.<br /> <br /> Everything in the world of darkness wants you dead and your gnosis goes down by the day(meaning at the end of a week you'll have anywhere from 1-3, not nearly enough to use your gifts properly when fighting off everything else), you have half dice pools(even at will 10 you don't have enough WP to spend every hour, you'd burn out in the first day), and you have nowhere to hide as the cities are owned by the vampires and the forests are owned by the garou.<br /> <br /> You can't learn any new disciplines without a teacher(save the physical ones, and possible clan depending how you read it), and the one you have is most likely already dead(your sire when you first wake is a vampire who just cursed you to be an abomination against gaia for eternity, you're either restrained in a basement and not learning any disciplines or he's ashes). The only way for said abomination to be badass is if it gave up it's free will to the wyrm, in which case it's literally a robot that shut's down the moment it can't get commands.<br /> <br /> So the only surviving abominations are weaker than a normal werwolf and strapped to someones basement or maeljin incarna that are being driven around by the wyrm itself(meaning it'll be as powerful as you want it to be anyway, not powerful because abominations are powerful).<br /> <br /> They're purposely written to be either crap or &quot;plot device&quot; meaning while their potential is great, they either don't live up to it or it doesn't matter because they're a plot device character that has whatever powers an ST feels like giving them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T18:26:40-08:00","id":1157843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1136473-abominations?p=1157776#post1157776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abominations do have a good concept, but they are more useful as storyteller-device than actual player characters. They are actually powerful and even the book authors agree with that, it's a fact. For example, an Abomination with only Celerity 5 is already very powerful (you can soak any type of damage if you're in a form that's not your breed; and any form if you're Metis. Plus, you can have 5 extra actions instead of a maximum of permanent Rage rating/2. You also can remain active. If you don't spend extra actions you already have +5 dice to your Dexterity-related actions; believe me, that's a lot of dicepool). Not to mention if the said Abomination had Spirit of the Fray or any other Gift that's alike, it would make them really unbeatable in combat (could probably even take on an experienced werewolf elder on a one versus one combat). Adding an Abomination as a player character can really break the game if it's not monitored and started properly, that's just my little humble opinion and I respect yours as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>The authors aren't all-knowing. Just because they think it is too powerful doesn't mean it is a fact. Look at the Abomination with Celerity 5. How did this Abomination <u>got</u> Celerity 5? What could it had got instead if it was only a Werewolf? Or what could it get as a Vampire without spending XP on Spirit of the Fray?<br /> <br /> It is not that an Abomination can't get nice combos, and certainly they need some attention as PCs. But it is doable without much of a problem. Except for the damn rule on Gnosis that leaves them mostly unplayable if not house-ruled out, along with permanent Harano. Adding Disciplines to a character's options is still just adding options, not giving power for free.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T13:30:10-08:00","id":1158265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1136473-abominations?p=1157843#post1157843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The authors aren't all-knowing. Just because they think it is too powerful doesn't mean it is a fact. Look at the Abomination with Celerity 5. How did this Abomination <u>got</u> Celerity 5? What could it had got instead if it was only a Werewolf? Or what could it get as a Vampire without spending XP on Spirit of the Fray?<br /> <br /> It is not that an Abomination can't get nice combos, and certainly they need some attention as PCs. But it is doable without much of a problem. Except for the damn rule on Gnosis that leaves them mostly unplayable if not house-ruled out, along with permanent Harano. Adding Disciplines to a character's options is still just adding options, not giving power for free.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was speaking in theory, although just because you spend in order to achieve power that does not really nullify the argument. It still stands the same. I for one don't really see much potential in having player character Abominations in my games, it would probably just make it hard for the person whose roleplaying the specified Abomination. I do understand the fact that there is an interesting concept after the embrace of a Werewolf, but that concept doesn't really last long especially when everyone in the game wants to get rid of you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1136473-abominations?p=1157793#post1157793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, Rage doesn't technically cap the number of actions that you can get, just the points that you can spend. This is an important distinction when you get to a Gift like Rage of the Many-Taloned Hunter, which counts each Rage point you spend to gain extra actions as two. The principle limit, however, is still the lower of Dexterity or Wits (or just Dexterity in a frenzy), since moving faster than your coordination can manage inflicts a +3 difficulty penalty to all your rolls for that turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant that as in the maximum amount of Rage points that are available to be spent in a single turn, didn't pay much attention when I wrote that. I was comparing that to spending blood for extra actions through Celerity. (which isn't capped by generation)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11698,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11698-darko","user":"Darko","date":". 11-13-2017, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11698-darko","name":"Darko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11698_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T18:17:50-08:00","id":1158307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1136473-abominations?p=1158265#post1158265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was speaking in theory, although just because you spend in order to achieve power that does not really nullify the argument. It still stands the same. I for one don't really see much potential in having player character Abominations in my games, it would probably just make it hard for the person whose roleplaying the specified Abomination. I do understand the fact that there is an interesting concept after the embrace of a Werewolf, but that concept doesn't really last long especially when everyone in the game wants to get rid of you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why go out of your way just to make a player miserable? I help my players to implement their ideas instead of forcing them into my safe zone, and I'm usually rewarded with experiences I didn't expected. Concepts and role-play opportunities I hadn't thought off myself. And if I really dislike something, I just talk to the player to get rid of the problem. I find no fun at all in punishing a player's choice in game.<br /> <br /> I didn't expected my player to want an Abomination when it happened. She wanted to do, she told me the background, she was excited with the concept of the character. I could have just denied it. She wouldn't like it, but she would accept, and play something else. I worked with her to make a few adjustments to place the character in the chronicle, instead. Got rid of the two rules that make such a character completely unplayable, the constant Harano and Gnosis Sink Hole. Otherwise, she had to follow the rules of both Humanity and the Gaian Garou just to keep madness away. She choose to start play with Disciplines, being Embraced when she was still a cub, so she could buy Gifts only with BP or XP.<br /> <br /> And it was a great chronicle, in no small part because of that character. She added drama, but could stir the sympathy of the other PCs, she walked a thin line between three worlds, Mortal, Garou and Kindred, with the lesser degree of direct contact being with the one she wanted more to be part with. It worked, and I'm fond of the decision I made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T13:54:31-08:00","id":1159167,"title":"","content":"Sounds like you made the right choice, monteparnas. You know your game and players better than randos on the internet do, and it sounds like you were able to weave the Abomination PC into your story with a deft touch. Not sure I could do it, but it gets the brain-juices flowing, just the same.<br /> <br /> The more I think about it the more I like the idea of serious vampire/Garou crossover. I like the idea of righteous Gaians being forced to interact with Damned that they can't (or won't!) destroy on sight. Perhaps they just bite their tongues and bide their time, or maybe they re-examine their own beliefs. Maybe they compromise too much, and get too familiar with the walking corpses. In any case, I think there is a lot of potential, one that is often ignored or abandoned because rage is a hell of a drug and vampires can make for easy punching bags.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}